# LongCat 2.5 Preview — SELF-EXCLUDED from scored findings (Step 5 Preview)

- Source: Meituan LongCat (`meituan/longcat-2.5-preview`)
- Date: 2026-10-09 (UTC)
- Reason for exclusion: **zero verified public benchmarks exist for this model** — Meituan published no benchmark table, Artificial Analysis does not track it, and no independent evaluation has been run. No scored findings file was written; the roster entry carries a placeholder Overall.

## What is verified about the model

- Meituan LongCat team released LongCat-2.5-Preview on its own API platform on **2026-09-25** (changelog: "Version: 2026-09-25 — LongCat-2.5-Preview Now Available"), preview status only.
- Architecture (vendor X account + launch coverage): sparse MoE, **~1.6T total parameters, ~48B active per token**, **1M-token context** (1,048,576), up to **131,072 max output** (some launch coverage says 128K).
- Modality: marketed as "natively multimodal" with new image understanding (text + image in; video by URL per launch coverage) → text out — but Meituan's own docs example for the model-metadata endpoint returns `input_modalities: ["text"]`, so the vision claim is unreconciled with the vendor's own API schema.
- Thinking on by default (per-request `thinking` toggle); tool calling; interleaved reasoning traces; "deep compatibility" with Claude Code, OpenCode, Kilo Code, OpenClaw and Hermes. OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible APIs at `api.longcat.chat`.
- Pricing: **$0.30/M input, $1.20/M output, $0.006/M cached input** (vendor "limited-time discounted" rate; list $0.75/$2.95 via some BYOK routes). Free for ~2 weeks on OpenCode Zen as `longcat-2.5-preview-free` (zero data retention).
- No weights published this generation (LongCat-2.0's MIT weights on the meituan-longcat org remain the last release; newest org repo is LongCat-Flash-Lite-Sparse, 2026-07-31).
- Usage signal (OpenCode data, updated 2026-10-08): #7 model by tokens last week (2.2T tokens, 0.5% share), 110K unique users, 5.12M completed sessions, 71.4% weekly retention, 95.4% of input tokens served from cache.
- Predecessor reference (not transferable): LongCat-2.0 (open weights, trained on Ascend 910B) was reported at 59.5 SWE-bench Pro at its July launch.

## What is missing (why exclusion)

- No vendor benchmark of any kind (no SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, MCP Atlas, GPQA, Arena) — the changelog only claims "superior" coding qualitatively.
- No Artificial Analysis page/Intelligence Index, no third-party eval; scores circulating on social media do not trace to a Meituan source.
- No model card, technical report, license, parameter table or dated snapshots; the model id has no version suffix.

## Re-score trigger

When Meituan (or an independent tracker) publishes a benchmark table, an AA listing appears, or an independent harness eval is run, write a normal `Step_5_Preview.md` for this slug covering Tool use, Reasoning, Context window, Multimodal, Coding, Cost efficiency and Overall per the methodology.

